       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin in adults. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the limit.\n\nHere are some options within the label:\n- **Immediate-release, 850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Immediate-release, 1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **Extended-release, 2,000 mg once daily with the evening meal.** This is the usual ER maximum.\n\nIf 1700 mg was a typo, for example for 850 mg or 500 mg, tell me the intended dose and formulation. If you want a different dose or schedule, I can enter that instead."
      }
